  "system": {
    "slug": "cerberus-guardian",
    "details": {
      "level": {
        "value": 5
      },
      "publicNotes": "<p>Cerberus Guardians are heavily armored infantry equipped with a large ballistic tower shield that makes them nearly invulnerable to frontal attacks. They advance slowly but relentlessly, providing a mobile barrier for allied forces behind them. Targeting the sliver of exposed visor or flanking around the shield are the primary methods to defeat them efficiently.</p><p><strong>Tower Shield:</strong> The Guardian has +4 AC vs. ranged attacks from their front arc and is immune to area effects from that direction. Melee attackers in the Guardian's front arc must succeed on a DC 22 Reflex save or be knocked back 5 feet.</p><p><strong>Shield Bash (reaction):</strong> When an adjacent creature attacks the Guardian in melee, the Guardian may make one Shield Bash attack as a reaction (+14 to hit, 2d4+4 bludgeoning, Push 10 ft).</p>",
      "privateNotes": "",
      "publication": {
        "title": "Mass Effect Compendium",
        "authors": "nscarpinatodev",
        "license": "ORC",
        "remaster": true
      },
      "languages": {
        "value": [],
        "details": ""
      },
      "blurb": "Heavily armored Cerberus trooper with a tower ballistic shield, nearly impervious to frontal attacks."
